   "title": "How to use · v2.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v2.0.0\n\n**What it does:** makes a picture from a text prompt with MiniMax H3 Image, on the 12 GB files, in one node. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Prompt**: describe the whole picture like a photo caption: subject, place, light, lens, colours. Long, exact prompts work best. Text in quotes is drawn as text. There is no negative prompt.\n2. **Shape / Megapixels**: 7.5 MP default, 3424x2304 at 3:2. MiniMax built the model for 4 to 20 MP.\n3. **Seed**: new number = new picture.\n4. **Run**. The picture is saved to `output/MiniMax-H3-Image/`.\n\n**6 steps, CFG 1** are fixed inside the node: MiniMax distilled this checkpoint to exactly that. More steps or a higher CFG do not make it better.\n\n**No Turbo mode here, on purpose.** I tested the 2-step pDMD LoRA (made for H3 video) on the RTX 3060: 22 s instead of 44 s, but soft with a visible grid pattern, and the grid was still there at 4 steps and at 4 MP.\n\n| RTX 3060 12 GB, 7.5 MP | Time |\n|---|---|\n| models unloaded first | 66 s |\n| new prompt, models used before | 59 s |\n| same prompt, new seed | 44 s |\n\nSame picture as v1.0.0 for the same seed (checked pixel by pixel). Double-click the node to see every step.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX 3060 12 GB · 32 GB RAM · ComfyUI 0.45.3.\n"
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
